                <pb facs="0326" n="314" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg314"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Argentina/197: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-05-12T13:00:00-04:00">May 12, 1942—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>656. From Metals Reserve. Your 825, May 5, 11 p.m.</p>
                <p>“Metals Reserve is prepared to make the Saba contract effective contingent upon
                    the Argentine Government granting export licenses for export to the United
                    States of the accumulated stocks of beryl ore and a further agreement to grant
                    licenses at the rate of a minimum of 100 tons of ore monthly out of current
                    production. Since the consumption of the Saba plant will be only about 1,000
                    tons of ore per year, export licenses should be granted for any quantity in
                    excess of this requirement of Saba but not less than 1,200 tons annually.”</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
